{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.6,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "bridged_nets",
      "components": ["U2", "J2", "DISPLAY sheet symbol"],
      "pins": ["U2.30", "U2.35", "J2.4"],
      "nets": ["NET0009"],
      "observed": "On the root sheet (PCB.kicad_sch) the net label NET0009 is attached to MCU pin PA14 (the SWCLK line that also feeds J2 pin 4), and the same label NET0009 is used on the bottom pin of the DISPLAY hierarchical sheet symbol, whose wire runs to MCU pin PB14. The two pins are therefore merged onto one net.",
      "expected": "Per the spec, PA14 is SWCLK (debug clock) and PB14 is DISP_SDA (OLED data). These are unrelated signals and must not share a net: 'DISP_SDA: U2 pin 35 (PB14)' and the SWD clock is a separate debug line.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "Root sheet: PA14 (pin 30) carries label NET0009; J2 SWCLK pin carries NET0009; DISPLAY sheet-symbol bottom pin carries NET0009 wired to PB14 (pin 35)"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "DISP_SDA: U2 pin 35 (PB14) — R7 (10 kΩ) to VCC — U4 pins 19/20 (D1/D2)"}
      ],
      "impact": "SWCLK is shorted to the OLED SDA line, corrupting the I2C bus and preventing reliable SWD programming; the MCU cannot drive either function correctly.",
      "confidence": 0.6
    },
    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": ["U2", "U1 (ER-OLED0.96-1W)", "DISPLAY sheet symbol"],
      "pins": ["U2.34", "U2.35", "U1.18", "U1.19", "U1.20"],
      "nets": ["NET0016", "NET0018", "NET0012"],
      "observed": "The DISPLAY sheet symbol on the root sheet is labelled NET0002 / NET0016 / NET0009, but the display sub-sheet (display.kicad_sch) drives its SCL/SDA pins with the labels NET0018 (D0) and NET0012 (D1/D2). Only NET0002 (RES#) matches; the two data nets on the root symbol (NET0016, NET0009) have no counterpart inside the sheet, and the sheet's NET0018/NET0012 have no counterpart on the root.",
      "expected": "A hierarchical sheet symbol's pin labels must match the hierarchical/global labels inside the sub-sheet so the OLED SCL and SDA reach PB13/PB14. Spec: 'DISP_SCL: U2 pin 34 (PB13) ... U4 pin 18 (D0)' and 'DISP_SDA: U2 pin 35 (PB14) ... U4 pins 19/20'.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "Root sheet DISPLAY symbol: NET0002, NET0016, NET0009; display.kicad_sch: RES#=NET0002, D0/D1 line=NET0018, D2 line=NET0012"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "DISP_SCL: U2 pin 34 (PB13) — R6 (10 kΩ) to VCC — U4 pin 18 (D0)"}
      ],
      "impact": "The OLED SCL and SDA signals never connect to the MCU, so the display cannot be addressed over I2C (only its reset line is wired).",
      "confidence": 0.55
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Power, NFC, touch and SWD blocks match the specification, but the DISPLAY interface is broken: the root-sheet sheet-symbol labels (NET0016/NET0009) do not match the display sub-sheet's actual nets (NET0018/NET0012), leaving SCL/SDA open, and the reused NET0009 additionally shorts the SWCLK net to the MCU pin wired to the display symbol (PB14)."
}

